INT. CHEESE CAVE - NIGHT

Cold. Wet stone. Racks of aging wheels in rows. A single utility bulb.

LUCA FERRANTE, 40s, crowbar in hand. TAMAR ELKAYAM, 30s, holds a flashlight. BRODIE MACLEAN, 20s, hauls a sack.

LUCA
Which wheel?

TAMAR
Third rack. The black wax.

BRODIE
It all looks black.

TAMAR
The one that smells like feet.

Brodie sniffs. Gags. Points.

BRODIE
That one.

Luca wedges the crowbar under the wheel. It pops free. Inside, a hollow core and a small steel case.

LUCA
Got it.

A flashlight swings in from the entrance. RHIANNON DAVIES, 30s, in a hairnet and rubber boots, a nightwatch's baton in her fist, steps from the dark.

RHIANNON
Evening.

They freeze. Tamar lowers the light. Brodie drops the sack.

RHIANNON (CONT'D)
That wheel's forty thousand euros.

TAMAR
We'll pay for it.

RHIANNON
Not with cash.

She steps forward. She holds out her free hand. Luca hands her the steel case.

LUCA
You knew.

RHIANNON
I run this cave, mate.

She slides the case under her arm. Tamar, Luca, and Brodie exchange looks. Nobody moves. Water drips somewhere.

BRODIE
So are we fired?

RHIANNON
You were never hired.
